# Vercel CLI reads this file *instead of* .gitignore when it exists, and that
# inversion is why every secret is named here explicitly: Next loads
# `.env.local` at build time and it would quietly override the environment set
# in the Vercel project — starting with APP_URL, which is still localhost there.
#
# `/public/uploads/` used to be force-shipped from here: it is git-ignored, and
# the catalogue still pointed at files uploaded before media moved to Supabase
# Storage, so a deployment without them was a shop of grey rectangles. Those
# files were deleted on 2026-08-19 and the references cleared with them — every
# photograph now lives in the bucket, and nothing needs carrying along.

node_modules
.next
.git

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*credentials*
.admin-credentials.local
*.secret

# Tests never run on the deployment.
*.test.ts

# Legacy file-backed store, superseded by Postgres.
data

# Local backups (`npm run backup`). In `.gitignore` too, which is not enough:
# this file *replaces* that one rather than adding to it, so anything listed
# only there still ships. `backup/` is 48 MB of product photographs and a dump
# of `orders` — customer names, telephones and addresses — and none of it has
# any business in a deployment.
backup

.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.vercel

# Build output of other tools. None of these exists today; they are named
# because the cost of listing a directory that never appears is nothing, and
# the cost of shipping one is another upload like `backup/` was.
out
build
